/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL - Ezekiel chapters 31-35
   Verse text intentionally left empty (verse:"") per build spec */
VG.registerBibleChapters("ezekiel", [
{n:31, name:"The Fall of the Cedar", seal:{ref:"Ezekiel 31:18",verse:"To whom art thou thus like in glory and in greatness among the trees of Eden? yet shalt thou be brought down with the trees of Eden unto the nether parts of the earth: thou shalt lie in the midst of the uncircumcised with them that be slain by the sword. This is Pharaoh and all his multitude, saith the Lord GOD."}, facts:["Did you know this oracle against Pharaoh is dated to the eleventh year, in the third month, on the first day of the month (Ezekiel 31:1)?","Did you know God says He Himself made the cedar fair, so that all the trees of Eden, that were in the garden of God, envied him (Ezekiel 31:9)?","Did you know the chapter ends by naming the cedar plainly: This is Pharaoh and all his multitude, saith the Lord GOD (Ezekiel 31:18)?"], questions:[
{q:"When did the word of the LORD come to Ezekiel in this chapter?", options:["In the eleventh year, in the third month, in the first day of the month","In the twelfth year, in the twelfth month","In the fifth year of the captivity","In the year Jerusalem fell"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:1",verse:"And it came to pass in the eleventh year, in the third month, in the first day of the month, that the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,", insight:"God dates His warnings; judgment arrives on a schedule, not by accident."},
{q:"To whom was Ezekiel told to speak this word?", options:["Pharaoh king of Egypt, and to his multitude","The king of Babylon and his princes","The elders of Israel in captivity","The priests of the temple"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:2",verse:"Son of man, speak unto Pharaoh king of Egypt, and to his multitude; Whom art thou like in thy greatness?", insight:"God's word goes straight to the throne; no power is above the message."},
{q:"What searching question was put to Pharaoh?", options:["Whom art thou like in thy greatness?","Where is thy god, O Pharaoh?","How long wilt thou resist the LORD?","What is thy name among the nations?"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:2",verse:"Son of man, speak unto Pharaoh king of Egypt, and to his multitude; Whom art thou like in thy greatness?", insight:"Greatness invites comparison; God asks the proud to measure themselves honestly."},
{q:"To what was the Assyrian compared?", options:["A cedar in Lebanon with fair branches, of an high stature","An eagle soaring over the mountains","A lion among the beasts of the field","A tower reaching up to heaven"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:3",verse:"Behold, the Assyrian was a cedar in Lebanon with fair branches, and with a shadowing shroud, and of an high stature; and his top was among the thick boughs.", insight:"Assyria the cedar: empires look eternal until the axe is lifted."},
{q:"What made the cedar great?", options:["The waters made him great, and the deep set him up on high","The favor of Pharaoh and his armies","The worship of the nations round about","The gold stored in his treasuries"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:4",verse:"The waters made him great, the deep set him up on high with her rivers running round about his plants, and sent out her little rivers unto all the trees of the field.", insight:"Greatness borrowed from deep waters; forget the source and the top will tremble."},
{q:"How tall did the cedar stand among the trees?", options:["His height was exalted above all the trees of the field","He was lowly among the shrubs","He stood level with the fir trees","He was hidden beneath the thick boughs"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:5",verse:"Therefore his height was exalted above all the trees of the field, and his boughs were multiplied, and his branches became long because of the multitude of waters, when he shot forth.", insight:"To tower above all the trees is glory until it becomes pride."},
{q:"Who made their nests in the cedar's boughs?", options:["All the fowls of heaven","The doves of the temple","The sparrows of the field only","No bird would rest in him"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:6",verse:"All the fowls of heaven made their nests in his boughs, and under his branches did all the beasts of the field bring forth their young, and under his shadow dwelt all great nations.", insight:"Nations nested in Assyria's branches; power always gathers dependents."},
{q:"Why was the cedar fair in his greatness and in the length of his branches?", options:["For his root was by great waters","For his leaves never withered","For the kings watered him","For the sun shone only on him"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:7",verse:"Thus was he fair in his greatness, in the length of his branches: for his root was by great waters.", insight:"Rooted by great waters; every towering life is fed by something deeper than itself."},
{q:"Who dwelt under the cedar's shadow?", options:["All great nations","Only the poor and lowly","The priests and Levites","No man dared approach him"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:6",verse:"All the fowls of heaven made their nests in his boughs, and under his branches did all the beasts of the field bring forth their young, and under his shadow dwelt all great nations.", insight:"All great nations sheltered there; fallen empires leave many standing in the open."},
{q:"How did the trees of the garden of God compare with him?", options:["None was like unto him in his beauty","They were fairer by far","They despised his branches","They could not see him at all"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:8",verse:"The cedars in the garden of God could not hide him: the fir trees were not like his boughs, and the chesnut trees were not like his branches; nor any tree in the garden of God was like unto him in his beauty.", insight:"Surpassing even Eden's trees; beauty is a gift, not a shield."},
{q:"What did the trees of Eden do when God made him fair?", options:["They envied him","They praised him","They bowed down before him","They withered away"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:9",verse:"I have made him fair by the multitude of his branches: so that all the trees of Eden, that were in the garden of God, envied him.", insight:"Envy even in Eden; gifts from God can stir jealousy in others and pride in us."},
{q:"Why did the LORD pronounce judgment on the cedar?", options:["His heart was lifted up in his height","His roots had dried up","His branches bore no fruit","The nations had forsaken him"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:10",verse:"Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Because thou hast lifted up thyself in height, and he hath shot up his top among the thick boughs, and his heart is lifted up in his height;", insight:"The lifted heart is the beginning of the fall; pride writes its own sentence."},
{q:"Into whose hand was the proud cedar delivered?", options:["The hand of the mighty one of the heathen","The hand of the priests of Israel","The hand of Pharaoh himself","The hand of the prophets"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:11",verse:"I have therefore delivered him into the hand of the mighty one of the heathen; he shall surely deal with him: I have driven him out for his wickedness.", insight:"God uses one proud power to humble another; He is never short of instruments."},
{q:"Who cut the cedar off and left him?", options:["Strangers, the terrible of the nations","His own gardeners","The fowls of heaven","A sudden storm from the sea"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:12",verse:"And strangers, the terrible of the nations, have cut him off, and have left him: upon the mountains and in all the valleys his branches are fallen, and his boughs are broken by all the rivers of the land; and all the people of the earth are gone down from his shadow, and have left him.", insight:"Terrible strangers with axes; what pride built, violence dismantles."},
{q:"Where did his branches fall and break?", options:["Upon the mountains and in all the valleys, by all the rivers of the land","Only in the garden of God","Into the depths of the sea","Upon the walls of Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:12",verse:"And strangers, the terrible of the nations, have cut him off, and have left him: upon the mountains and in all the valleys his branches are fallen, and his boughs are broken by all the rivers of the land; and all the people of the earth are gone down from his shadow, and have left him.", insight:"Branches scattered over mountain and valley; the fall of the great is never private."},
{q:"What remained upon his ruin?", options:["All the fowls of the heaven and all the beasts of the field","The gardeners who tended him","The kings who had honored him","Nothing living at all"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:13",verse:"Upon his ruin shall all the fowls of the heaven remain, and all the beasts of the field shall be upon his branches:", insight:"Birds and beasts on the ruin; glory gone, only scavengers keep court."},
{q:"What was the purpose of the cedar's fall?", options:["That none of the trees by the waters exalt themselves for their height","That Lebanon might grow richer","That the rivers might run dry","That the beasts might find new pasture"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:14",verse:"To the end that none of all the trees by the waters exalt themselves for their height, neither shoot up their top among the thick boughs, neither their trees stand up in their height, all that drink water: for they are all delivered unto death, to the nether parts of the earth, in the midst of the children of men, with them that go down to the pit.", insight:"A warning to every towering tree: what happened to Assyria can happen to you."},
{q:"What did God do in the day the cedar went down to the grave?", options:["He caused a mourning, covered the deep, and restrained the floods","He sent rain upon Lebanon","He planted a new cedar at once","He hid the news from the nations"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:15",verse:"Thus saith the Lord GOD; In the day when he went down to the grave I caused a mourning: I covered the deep for him, and I restrained the floods thereof, and the great waters were stayed: and I caused Lebanon to mourn for him, and all the trees of the field fainted for him.", insight:"Even heaven mourned the fall; God takes no glee in the ruin of the great."},
{q:"Who went down into hell with him?", options:["They that were his arm, that dwelt under his shadow","The trees of Eden alone","The fowls of heaven","None followed him down"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:17",verse:"They also went down into hell with him unto them that be slain with the sword; and they that were his arm, that dwelt under his shadow in the midst of the heathen.", insight:"His arm went with him; those who lean on pride share its grave."},
{q:"To whom does this parable of the cedar apply?", options:["This is Pharaoh and all his multitude, saith the Lord GOD","This is Nebuchadnezzar and Babylon","This is the king of Tyre and his merchants","This is Israel and her elders"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 31:18",verse:"To whom art thou thus like in glory and in greatness among the trees of Eden? yet shalt thou be brought down with the trees of Eden unto the nether parts of the earth: thou shalt lie in the midst of the uncircumcised with them that be slain by the sword. This is Pharaoh and all his multitude, saith the Lord GOD.", insight:"Pharaoh, look at Assyria and learn; the cedar's fall is your mirror."}
]},
{n:32, name:"A Lament for Pharaoh", seal:{ref:"Ezekiel 32:15",verse:"When I shall make the land of Egypt desolate, and the country shall be destitute of that whereof it was full, when I shall smite all them that dwell therein, then shall they know that I am the LORD."}, facts:["Did you know Pharaoh is pictured as both a young lion of the nations and a whale in the seas within a single lament (Ezekiel 32:2)?","Did you know the pit already holds Asshur, Elam, Meshech, Tubal, Edom, the princes of the north, and the Zidonians, all lying there to greet Pharaoh (Ezekiel 32:22)?","Did you know God says Egypt's rivers will one day run like oil, still and quiet after the terror is past (Ezekiel 32:14)?"], questions:[
{q:"When did this lamentation for Pharaoh come?", options:["In the twelfth year, in the twelfth month, in the first day of the month","In the eleventh year, in the third month","In the tenth month of the captivity","In the year of Pharaoh's birth"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:1",verse:"And it came to pass in the twelfth year, in the twelfth month, in the first day of the month, that the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,", insight:"A dated lament; God keeps a calendar for the fall of kings."},
{q:"What was Ezekiel told to take up for Pharaoh?", options:["A lamentation","A song of triumph","A covenant of peace","A blessing for his reign"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:2",verse:"Son of man, take up a lamentation for Pharaoh king of Egypt, and say unto him, Thou art like a young lion of the nations, and thou art as a whale in the seas: and thou camest forth with thy rivers, and troubledst the waters with thy feet, and fouledst their rivers.", insight:"A lamentation, not a war cry; even God's judgment on Egypt is sung with sorrow."},
{q:"To what two creatures is Pharaoh compared?", options:["A young lion of the nations, and a whale in the seas","An eagle and a serpent","A bull and a bear","A horse and a chariot"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:2",verse:"Son of man, take up a lamentation for Pharaoh king of Egypt, and say unto him, Thou art like a young lion of the nations, and thou art as a whale in the seas: and thou camest forth with thy rivers, and troubledst the waters with thy feet, and fouledst their rivers.", insight:"Lion on land, whale in the sea; Pharaoh claimed every domain, and God would empty them all."},
{q:"What command is given to Egypt as she goes down to the pit?", options:["Go down, and be thou laid with the uncircumcised","Rise up, and take thy throne again","Flee to the mountains and hide","Call upon thy gods for help"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:19",verse:"Whom dost thou pass in beauty? go down, and be thou laid with the uncircumcised.", insight:"Laid with the uncircumcised; pride's end is a grave among the godless."},
{q:"What will God spread over Pharaoh?", options:["His net, with a company of many people","A cloud of darkness","A banner of war","A veil over his eyes"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:3",verse:"Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will therefore spread out my net over thee with a company of many people; and they shall bring thee up in my net.", insight:"Caught in God's net; the hunter of nations becomes the hunted."},
{q:"Where will God leave Pharaoh?", options:["Upon the land, cast forth upon the open field","In the depths of the sea","Within the walls of his palace","In the land of Canaan"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:4",verse:"Then will I leave thee upon the land, I will cast thee forth upon the open field, and will cause all the fowls of the heaven to remain upon thee, and I will fill the beasts of the whole earth with thee.", insight:"Left on the open field; the whale out of water is a warning to all."},
{q:"What will God do with Pharaoh's flesh?", options:["Lay it upon the mountains, and fill the valleys with his height","Bury it with honor in Egypt","Cast it into the deep sea","Burn it with fire"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:5",verse:"And I will lay thy flesh upon the mountains, and fill the valleys with thy height.", insight:"Mountains and valleys covered; pride that filled the land will litter it."},
{q:"How far would his blood water the land?", options:["Even to the mountains","Only around his palace","To the borders of Canaan","Nowhere at all"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:6",verse:"I will also water with thy blood the land wherein thou swimmest, even to the mountains; and the rivers shall be full of thee.", insight:"Blood to the mountains; the scale of the judgment matches the scale of the pride."},
{q:"What will happen in the heavens at his fall?", options:["The sun covered with a cloud, the stars dark, the moon giving no light","A new star appearing in glory","The heavens opened with joy","Nothing will change above"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:7",verse:"And when I shall put thee out, I will cover the heaven, and make the stars thereof dark; I will cover the sun with a cloud, and the moon shall not give her light.", insight:"Darkened heavens for a darkened king; creation itself mourns the wreck of pride."},
{q:"How will the kings react in the day of Pharaoh's fall?", options:["They shall be horribly afraid, and tremble every man for his own life","They will rejoice and feast","They will crown a new Pharaoh","They will ignore the news"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:10",verse:"Yea, I will make many people amazed at thee, and their kings shall be horribly afraid for thee, when I shall brandish my sword before them; and they shall tremble at every moment, every man for his own life, in the day of thy fall.", insight:"Kings trembling for their own lives; one throne's fall shakes every throne."},
{q:"Whose sword shall come upon Pharaoh?", options:["The sword of the king of Babylon","The sword of the king of Assyria","The sword of his own servants","The sword of the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:11",verse:"For thus saith the Lord GOD; The sword of the king of Babylon shall come upon thee.", insight:"Babylon's sword: God names the instrument long before it strikes."},
{q:"What will the terrible of the nations spoil?", options:["The pomp of Egypt","The temples of the gods","The ships of Tarshish","The vineyards of Canaan"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:12",verse:"By the swords of the mighty will I cause thy multitude to fall, the terrible of the nations, all of them: and they shall spoil the pomp of Egypt, and all the multitude thereof shall be destroyed.", insight:"The pomp of Egypt spoiled; pageantry cannot survive the sword."},
{q:"What will God destroy from beside the great waters?", options:["All the beasts thereof","All the ships","All the fishermen","All the reeds"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:13",verse:"I will destroy also all the beasts thereof from beside the great waters; neither shall the foot of man trouble them any more, nor the hoofs of beasts trouble them.", insight:"Even the cattle by the Nile; judgment touches everything the proud one owned."},
{q:"How will Egypt's rivers run after the judgment?", options:["Like oil","Like blood","Like honey","They will run dry"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:14",verse:"Then will I make their waters deep, and cause their rivers to run like oil, saith the Lord GOD.", insight:"Rivers like oil: a strange, still peace after the terror is gone."},
{q:"What will Egypt know when the land is made desolate?", options:["That I am the LORD","That Pharaoh is god","That Babylon is eternal","That the Nile is holy"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:15",verse:"When I shall make the land of Egypt desolate, and the country shall be destitute of that whereof it was full, when I shall smite all them that dwell therein, then shall they know that I am the LORD.", insight:"Desolation teaches what sermons could not: He is the LORD."},
{q:"Who shall lament for Egypt?", options:["The daughters of the nations","The sons of Pharaoh","The priests of Egypt","The armies of Babylon"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:16",verse:"This is the lamentation wherewith they shall lament her: the daughters of the nations shall lament her: they shall lament for her, even for Egypt, and for all her multitude, saith the Lord GOD.", insight:"The daughters of the nations will weep; even enemies are mourned by the world."},
{q:"When did the second word of this chapter come?", options:["In the twelfth year, in the fifteenth day of the month","In the first day of the month","In the eleventh year","In the tenth month"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:17",verse:"It came to pass also in the twelfth year, in the fifteenth day of the month, that the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,", insight:"Fifteen days later, another word; God repeats the warning before the fall."},
{q:"What was Ezekiel told to do for the multitude of Egypt?", options:["Wail for them, and cast them down to the nether parts of the earth","Bless them and send them away","Number them for battle","Hide them in the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:18",verse:"Son of man, wail for the multitude of Egypt, and cast them down, even her, and the daughters of the famous nations, unto the nether parts of the earth, with them that go down into the pit.", insight:"Wail for the multitude; the prophet weeps over those he warns."},
{q:"Which fallen power is named as already lying in the pit?", options:["Asshur and all her company","Judah and her kings","Tyre and her merchants","Moab and her princes"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:22",verse:"Asshur is there and all her company: his graves are about him: all of them slain, fallen by the sword:", insight:"Asshur is there; the grave already holds empires greater than Egypt."},
{q:"What small comfort will Pharaoh find in the pit?", options:["He shall see the fallen nations, and be comforted over all his multitude","He will be restored to his throne","He will be remembered with honor","He will find his gods waiting"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 32:31",verse:"Pharaoh shall see them, and shall be comforted over all his multitude, even Pharaoh and all his army slain by the sword, saith the Lord GOD.", insight:"Comforted by worse company; misery loves the company of the fallen."}
]},
{n:33, name:"The Watchman", seal:{ref:"Ezekiel 33:11",verse:"Say unto them, As I live, saith the Lord GOD, I have no pleasure in the death of the wicked; but that the wicked turn from his way and live: turn ye, turn ye from your evil ways; for why will ye die, O house of Israel?"}, facts:["Did you know God's heart is laid bare in one sentence here: I have no pleasure in the death of the wicked, but that the wicked turn from his way and live (Ezekiel 33:11)?","Did you know the fall of Jerusalem reached Ezekiel in Babylon through a single fugitive's three words: The city is smitten (Ezekiel 33:21)?","Did you know the people treated Ezekiel's warnings as entertainment, a very lovely song of one that hath a pleasant voice, hearing but never doing (Ezekiel 33:32)?"], questions:[
{q:"Whom do the people of a land set as their watchman when the sword comes?", options:["A man of their coasts","The king's eldest son","A priest from the temple","A soldier from the army"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:2",verse:"Son of man, speak to the children of thy people, and say unto them, When I bring the sword upon a land, if the people of the land take a man of their coasts, and set him for their watchman:", insight:"A man of their coasts: the watchman is chosen from among the people, not above them."},
{q:"What must the watchman do when he sees the sword come upon the land?", options:["Blow the trumpet, and warn the people","Shut the gates and hide","Flee to the mountains","Offer a sacrifice"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:3",verse:"If when he seeth the sword come upon the land, he blow the trumpet, and warn the people;", insight:"Blow the trumpet; the watchman's whole duty is warning, plain and loud."},
{q:"What happens to the one who hears the trumpet and takes no warning?", options:["His blood shall be upon his own head","The watchman shall die for him","He shall be forgiven anyway","The king shall pardon him"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:4",verse:"Then whosoever heareth the sound of the trumpet, and taketh not warning; if the sword come, and take him away, his blood shall be upon his own head.", insight:"Warned and unheeding, his blood is on his own head; grace refused becomes judgment deserved."},
{q:"What if the watchman sees the sword and blows not the trumpet?", options:["His blood will God require at the watchman's hand","Nothing will happen to anyone","The people will forgive him","The sword will turn aside"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:6",verse:"But if the watchman see the sword come, and blow not the trumpet, and the people be not warned; if the sword come, and take any person from among them, he is taken away in his iniquity; but his blood will I require at the watchman’s hand.", insight:"Silent watchmen answer for silent warnings; to see danger and say nothing is guilt."},
{q:"Whom did God set as a watchman unto the house of Israel?", options:["Ezekiel, the son of man","Jeremiah the prophet","Daniel in Babylon","The high priest"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:7",verse:"So thou, O son of man, I have set thee a watchman unto the house of Israel; therefore thou shalt hear the word at my mouth, and warn them from me.", insight:"Ezekiel the watchman; your calling may be to warn people who will not thank you."},
{q:"If the prophet warns the wicked and he does not turn, what is the prophet's reward?", options:["He hath delivered his soul","He shall share the wicked man's punishment","He must warn him again at once","He shall lose his office"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:9",verse:"Nevertheless, if thou warn the wicked of his way to turn from it; if he do not turn from his way, he shall die in his iniquity; but thou hast delivered thy soul.", insight:"Delivered his soul: faithfulness is measured by the warning given, not the response."},
{q:"What despairing question did the house of Israel ask?", options:["If our sins be upon us, and we pine away in them, how should we then live?","Where is the God of our fathers?","Who will fight for us now?","When will the captivity end?"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:10",verse:"Therefore, O thou son of man, speak unto the house of Israel; Thus ye speak, saying, If our transgressions and our sins be upon us, and we pine away in them, how should we then live?", insight:"Pining away under sin, they asked how to live; despair is often the door to repentance."},
{q:"What does God say about the death of the wicked?", options:["He has no pleasure in it, but desires that the wicked turn and live","He delights in it as justice","He has no thought about it","He leaves it to the watchman"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:11",verse:"Say unto them, As I live, saith the Lord GOD, I have no pleasure in the death of the wicked; but that the wicked turn from his way and live: turn ye, turn ye from your evil ways; for why will ye die, O house of Israel?", insight:"No pleasure in the death of the wicked; judgment is God's strange work, mercy His delight."},
{q:"What happens to the righteous man who trusts in his own righteousness and commits iniquity?", options:["All his righteousnesses shall not be remembered, and he shall die for his iniquity","His past righteousness will save him","He shall be forgiven without turning","He will be made a watchman"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:13",verse:"When I shall say to the righteous, that he shall surely live; if he trust to his own righteousness, and commit iniquity, all his righteousnesses shall not be remembered; but for his iniquity that he hath committed, he shall die for it.", insight:"Past righteousness is no armor for present sin; God judges the man you are, not the man you were."},
{q:"What must the repentant wicked man do to live?", options:["Restore the pledge, give again what he robbed, and walk in the statutes of life","Offer a thousand sacrifices","Build a new altar","Flee to another country"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:15",verse:"If the wicked restore the pledge, give again that he had robbed, walk in the statutes of life, without committing iniquity; he shall surely live, he shall not die.", insight:"Restore, repay, and walk rightly; true repentance puts its hands on what it stole."},
{q:"How many of the repentant man's sins shall be mentioned unto him?", options:["None","Half of them","Only the greatest","All but one"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:16",verse:"None of his sins that he hath committed shall be mentioned unto him: he hath done that which is lawful and right; he shall surely live.", insight:"None mentioned; when God forgives, He forgets on purpose."},
{q:"What did the children of Israel say about the way of the Lord?", options:["The way of the Lord is not equal","The way of the Lord is too hard","The way of the Lord is hidden","The way of the Lord is slow"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:17",verse:"Yet the children of thy people say, The way of the Lord is not equal: but as for them, their way is not equal.", insight:"They called God's way unequal; the fault was in their measuring, not His justice."},
{q:"How will God judge the house of Israel?", options:["Every one after his ways","All together as one nation","Only the priests and kings","By the deeds of their fathers"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:20",verse:"Yet ye say, The way of the Lord is not equal. O ye house of Israel, I will judge you every one after his ways.", insight:"Every one after his ways; no one hides in the crowd on judgment day."},
{q:"Who brought the news of Jerusalem's fall to Ezekiel?", options:["One that had escaped out of Jerusalem, saying, The city is smitten","A messenger from Babylon","A prophet from Judah","A soldier of Pharaoh"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:21",verse:"And it came to pass in the twelfth year of our captivity, in the tenth month, in the fifth day of the month, that one that had escaped out of Jerusalem came unto me, saying, The city is smitten.", insight:"One escaped soul with three words: The city is smitten."},
{q:"What happened to Ezekiel the morning the fugitive came?", options:["His mouth was opened, and he was no more dumb","He fell sick and could not speak","He was taken to Jerusalem","He wept until evening"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:22",verse:"Now the hand of the LORD was upon me in the evening, afore he that was escaped came; and had opened my mouth, until he came to me in the morning; and my mouth was opened, and I was no more dumb.", insight:"The dumb prophet speaks again; God's timing opens mouths exactly when the news arrives."},
{q:"What abominations did the people commit, yet claim the land?", options:["They ate with the blood, worshipped idols, shed blood, and defiled their neighbors' wives","They built altars to the LORD only","They kept the Sabbath strictly","They refused to eat unclean food"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:26",verse:"Ye stand upon your sword, ye work abomination, and ye defile every one his neighbour’s wife: and shall ye possess the land?", insight:"Blood, idols, and adultery, then shall ye possess the land? Sin forfeits what grace would give."},
{q:"What three fates await those left in the land?", options:["The sword, the beasts, and the pestilence","Famine, flood, and fire","Exile, slavery, and silence","War, plague, and earthquake"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:27",verse:"Say thou thus unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; As I live, surely they that are in the wastes shall fall by the sword, and him that is in the open field will I give to the beasts to be devoured, and they that be in the forts and in the caves shall die of the pestilence.", insight:"Sword, beasts, pestilence; nowhere in the land is safe from a holy God."},
{q:"How did the people receive Ezekiel's words?", options:["They heard his words, but they would not do them","They obeyed him at once","They drove him from the city","They wrote his words in a book"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:31",verse:"And they come unto thee as the people cometh, and they sit before thee as my people, and they hear thy words, but they will not do them: for with their mouth they shew much love, but their heart goeth after their covetousness.", insight:"Hearers but not doers; their mouths showed love while their hearts chased covetousness."},
{q:"What was Ezekiel to his hearers?", options:["As a very lovely song of one that hath a pleasant voice","As a thundering judge","As a silent stone","As a forgotten dream"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:32",verse:"And, lo, thou art unto them as a very lovely song of one that hath a pleasant voice, and can play well on an instrument: for they hear thy words, but they do them not.", insight:"A lovely song to entertained ears; truth treated as music never changes a life."},
{q:"What will they know when all this comes to pass?", options:["That a prophet hath been among them","That Ezekiel was mistaken","That the watchman slept","That the city still stands"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 33:33",verse:"And when this cometh to pass, (lo, it will come,) then shall they know that a prophet hath been among them.", insight:"Too late they will know; a prophet among them was God's mercy they called entertainment."}
]},
{n:34, name:"The True Shepherd", seal:{ref:"Ezekiel 34:23",verse:"And I will set up one shepherd over them, and he shall feed them, even my servant David; he shall feed them, and he shall be their shepherd."}, facts:["Did you know God promises one shepherd, my servant David, centuries after David's death, a promise Christians read as pointing to the Messiah (Ezekiel 34:23)?","Did you know the beloved phrase there shall be showers of blessing comes from God's promise to His scattered flock (Ezekiel 34:26)?","Did you know the bad shepherds are charged with five specific neglects: the diseased not strengthened, the sick not healed, the broken not bound up, the driven not brought back, the lost not sought (Ezekiel 34:4)?"], questions:[
{q:"What woe is pronounced at the start of this chapter?", options:["Woe be to the shepherds of Israel that do feed themselves","Woe to the prophets who prophesy lies","Woe to the rich men of Jerusalem","Woe to the nations round about"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:2",verse:"Son of man, prophesy against the shepherds of Israel, prophesy, and say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD unto the shepherds; Woe be to the shepherds of Israel that do feed themselves! should not the shepherds feed the flocks?", insight:"Woe to shepherds who feed themselves; leadership that feeds on the flock is cursed."},
{q:"What did the false shepherds do with the flock?", options:["They ate the fat, clothed themselves with the wool, killed them that are fed, but fed not the flock","They sold the sheep to the Egyptians","They led the sheep into the wilderness to die","They gave the flock to the wolves"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:3",verse:"Ye eat the fat, and ye clothe you with the wool, ye kill them that are fed: but ye feed not the flock.", insight:"They ate and wore and killed, but never fed; using people is the opposite of shepherding."},
{q:"What fivefold neglect are the shepherds charged with?", options:["The diseased not strengthened, the sick not healed, the broken not bound up, the driven not brought back, the lost not sought","The sheep not counted, not branded, not washed, not shorn, not sold","The lambs not weaned, not trained, not fed, not watered, not housed","The rams not chosen, not fed, not guarded, not led, not returned"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:4",verse:"The diseased have ye not strengthened, neither have ye healed that which was sick, neither have ye bound up that which was broken, neither have ye brought again that which was driven away, neither have ye sought that which was lost; but with force and with cruelty have ye ruled them.", insight:"Five things left undone; God keeps a ledger of neglected mercy."},
{q:"Why were the sheep scattered?", options:["Because there was no shepherd","Because of a great famine","Because the wolves multiplied","Because the sheep rebelled"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:5",verse:"And they were scattered, because there is no shepherd: and they became meat to all the beasts of the field, when they were scattered.", insight:"Scattered for lack of a shepherd; sheep without care become prey."},
{q:"Where did the sheep wander, with none to seek them?", options:["Through all the mountains, and upon every high hill","Through the streets of Jerusalem only","Into the land of Egypt","Down to the Red Sea"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:6",verse:"My sheep wandered through all the mountains, and upon every high hill: yea, my flock was scattered upon all the face of the earth, and none did search or seek after them.", insight:"Over mountain and hill, none sought them; God notices every wandering one."},
{q:"What does God declare against the shepherds?", options:["Behold, I am against the shepherds, and I will require my flock at their hand","I will bless the shepherds forever","I will give them larger flocks","I will make them kings"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:10",verse:"Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I am against the shepherds; and I will require my flock at their hand, and cause them to cease from feeding the flock; neither shall the shepherds feed themselves any more; for I will deliver my flock from their mouth, that they may not be meat for them.", insight:"'I am against the shepherds'; God Himself opposes leaders who devour."},
{q:"Who will search out the scattered sheep?", options:["The LORD Himself: Behold, I, even I, will both search my sheep, and seek them out","The elders of Israel","The king of Babylon","The neighboring nations"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:11",verse:"For thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I, even I, will both search my sheep, and seek them out.", insight:"'I, even I'; when shepherds fail, God does the shepherding Himself."},
{q:"From what kind of day will God deliver His sheep?", options:["The cloudy and dark day","The day of harvest","The Sabbath day","The day of the new moon"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:12",verse:"As a shepherd seeketh out his flock in the day that he is among his sheep that are scattered; so will I seek out my sheep, and will deliver them out of all places where they have been scattered in the cloudy and dark day.", insight:"Out of the cloudy and dark day; God finds His own in the worst weather."},
{q:"Where will God bring His gathered sheep?", options:["To their own land, to feed upon the mountains of Israel by the rivers","To the land of Egypt","To the wilderness of Sinai","To the cities of Babylon"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:13",verse:"And I will bring them out from the people, and gather them from the countries, and will bring them to their own land, and feed them upon the mountains of Israel by the rivers, and in all the inhabited places of the country.", insight:"Home to their own land; God's gathering always ends in belonging."},
{q:"What kind of pasture does God promise?", options:["A good pasture, a good fold, and a fat pasture upon the mountains of Israel","A barren field in the desert","A pasture shared with the wolves","A fold with no water"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:14",verse:"I will feed them in a good pasture, and upon the high mountains of Israel shall their fold be: there shall they lie in a good fold, and in a fat pasture shall they feed upon the mountains of Israel.", insight:"Good pasture and a good fold; God's care is generous, not barely enough."},
{q:"What will God do for His flock?", options:["He will feed His flock, and cause them to lie down","He will sell them to the highest bidder","He will scatter them further","He will leave them to the shepherds"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:15",verse:"I will feed my flock, and I will cause them to lie down, saith the Lord GOD.", insight:"Fed and made to lie down; rest is part of the Shepherd's promise."},
{q:"What will God do for the lost, the driven, the broken, and the sick?", options:["Seek the lost, bring again the driven, bind up the broken, strengthen the sick, but destroy the fat and the strong","Leave them where they lie","Punish them all alike","Give them to other shepherds"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:16",verse:"I will seek that which was lost, and bring again that which was driven away, and will bind up that which was broken, and will strengthen that which was sick: but I will destroy the fat and the strong; I will feed them with judgment.", insight:"Mercy for the weak, judgment for the fat and strong; the Shepherd knows the difference."},
{q:"Between whom will God judge?", options:["Between cattle and cattle, between the rams and the he goats","Between the shepherds only","Between Israel and the nations","Between the old and the young"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:17",verse:"And as for you, O my flock, thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I judge between cattle and cattle, between the rams and the he goats.", insight:"God judges within the flock too; not all who graze together are alike."},
{q:"What did the strong cattle do to the pasture and the waters?", options:["They trod down the residue of the pastures and fouled the waters with their feet","They shared them freely with the weak","They guarded them day and night","They left them untouched"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:18",verse:"Seemeth it a small thing unto you to have eaten up the good pasture, but ye must tread down with your feet the residue of your pastures? and to have drunk of the deep waters, but ye must foul the residue with your feet?", insight:"Trampling what others need; the strong answer for the leftovers they ruined."},
{q:"How did the fat cattle treat the diseased?", options:["They thrust with side and shoulder, and pushed them with their horns till they scattered them","They carried them on their backs","They fed them from the best pasture","They left them in peace"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:21",verse:"Because ye have thrust with side and with shoulder, and pushed all the diseased with your horns, till ye have scattered them abroad;", insight:"Pushed with horns till they scattered; bullying the weak is a sin God names."},
{q:"Whom will God set up as one shepherd over the flock?", options:["My servant David","Moses the lawgiver","Ezekiel the prophet","A new king from Babylon"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:23",verse:"And I will set up one shepherd over them, and he shall feed them, even my servant David; he shall feed them, and he shall be their shepherd.", insight:"One shepherd, David's greater Son; the promise outlives the exile."},
{q:"What will David be among them?", options:["A prince among them","A servant in the palace","A priest in the temple","A stranger in the land"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:24",verse:"And I the LORD will be their God, and my servant David a prince among them; I the LORD have spoken it.", insight:"David a prince among them; God's King dwells with His people, not above them."},
{q:"What covenant will God make with them?", options:["A covenant of peace, causing the evil beasts to cease out of the land","A covenant of war against Babylon","A covenant of silver and gold","A covenant with the nations"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:25",verse:"And I will make with them a covenant of peace, and will cause the evil beasts to cease out of the land: and they shall dwell safely in the wilderness, and sleep in the woods.", insight:"A covenant of peace; safety in the wilderness, sleep in the woods."},
{q:"What will God send down in its season?", options:["The shower, and there shall be showers of blessing","Hail and fire","A flood of waters","Darkness at noon"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:26",verse:"And I will make them and the places round about my hill a blessing; and I will cause the shower to come down in his season; there shall be showers of blessing.", insight:"Showers of blessing; grace falls like rain on God's good timing."},
{q:"What will God raise up for them?", options:["A plant of renown","A tower of strength","A wall of brass","A city of gold"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 34:29",verse:"And I will raise up for them a plant of renown, and they shall be no more consumed with hunger in the land, neither bear the shame of the heathen any more.", insight:"A plant of renown; no more hunger, no more shame among the nations."}
]},
{n:35, name:"Against Mount Seir", seal:{ref:"Ezekiel 35:15",verse:"As thou didst rejoice at the inheritance of the house of Israel, because it was desolate, so will I do unto thee: thou shalt be desolate, O mount Seir, and all Idumea, even all of it: and they shall know that I am the LORD."}, facts:["Did you know mount Seir is Edom, the land of Esau's descendants, judged here for a perpetual hatred against Israel (Ezekiel 35:5)?","Did you know Edom claimed, These two nations and these two countries shall be mine, and God answered, whereas the LORD was there (Ezekiel 35:10)?","Did you know God measures Edom's punishment by its own joy: As thou didst rejoice at the inheritance of the house of Israel, so will I do unto thee (Ezekiel 35:15)?"], questions:[
{q:"What came unto Ezekiel at the start of this chapter?", options:["The word of the LORD","A vision of the temple","A messenger from Edom","A dream in the night"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:1",verse:"Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,", insight:"The word of the LORD; every judgment begins with God speaking."},
{q:"Against whom was Ezekiel told to set his face and prophesy?", options:["Mount Seir","Mount Zion","Mount Carmel","Mount Sinai"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:2",verse:"Son of man, set thy face against mount Seir, and prophesy against it,", insight:"Set thy face against mount Seir; God names the enemy of His people without flinching."},
{q:"What did the LORD declare against mount Seir?", options:["I am against thee, and I will make thee most desolate","I will make thee a fruitful field","I will set my temple upon thee","I will bless thee forever"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:3",verse:"And say unto it, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, O mount Seir, I am against thee, and I will stretch out mine hand against thee, and I will make thee most desolate.", insight:"'I am against thee'; when God stands opposed, no fortress holds."},
{q:"What would God do to the cities of Seir?", options:["Lay them waste, and make the land desolate","Fill them with new inhabitants","Surround them with walls of brass","Give them to the children of Israel"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:4",verse:"I will lay thy cities waste, and thou shalt be desolate, and thou shalt know that I am the LORD.", insight:"Cities laid waste; hatred's homeland becomes a wasteland."},
{q:"What had Edom harbored against Israel?", options:["A perpetual hatred","A secret alliance","A forgotten friendship","A paid tribute"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:5",verse:"Because thou hast had a perpetual hatred, and hast shed the blood of the children of Israel by the force of the sword in the time of their calamity, in the time that their iniquity had an end:", insight:"A perpetual hatred; some grudges are nursed for generations until God judges them."},
{q:"When did Edom shed the blood of Israel by the sword?", options:["In the time of their calamity","In the days of their prosperity","During the feast of harvest","In the year of jubilee"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:5",verse:"Because thou hast had a perpetual hatred, and hast shed the blood of the children of Israel by the force of the sword in the time of their calamity, in the time that their iniquity had an end:", insight:"They struck in the time of calamity; kicking a fallen brother is a sin God remembers."},
{q:"What did God say He would prepare Edom unto?", options:["Blood, and blood shall pursue thee","Peace, and peace shall follow thee","Wealth, and wealth shall find thee","Honor among the nations"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:6",verse:"Therefore, as I live, saith the Lord GOD, I will prepare thee unto blood, and blood shall pursue thee: sith thou hast not hated blood, even blood shall pursue thee.", insight:"'Blood shall pursue thee'; the violence you love will hunt you down."},
{q:"Whom would God cut off from mount Seir?", options:["Him that passeth out and him that returneth","The priests and the Levites","The women and the children only","The strangers within the gates"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:7",verse:"Thus will I make mount Seir most desolate, and cut off from it him that passeth out and him that returneth.", insight:"None passing through; desolation so complete that no traveler crosses it."},
{q:"Where would the slain of Seir fall?", options:["In thy hills, and in thy valleys, and in all thy rivers","Only within the city gates","In the wilderness far away","Upon the mountains of Israel"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:8",verse:"And I will fill his mountains with his slain men: in thy hills, and in thy valleys, and in all thy rivers, shall they fall that are slain with the sword.", insight:"Hills, valleys, rivers filled with the slain; judgment covers the whole land."},
{q:"What would become of Edom's cities?", options:["Perpetual desolations, and they shall not return","They would be rebuilt greater than before","They would be given to Judah","They would become markets for all nations"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:9",verse:"I will make thee perpetual desolations, and thy cities shall not return: and ye shall know that I am the LORD.", insight:"Perpetual desolations; some ruins are God's final word."},
{q:"What did Edom say about the two nations and two countries?", options:["These shall be mine, and we will possess it","These belong to the LORD forever","We will defend them with our lives","We know nothing of them"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:10",verse:"Because thou hast said, These two nations and these two countries shall be mine, and we will possess it; whereas the LORD was there:", insight:"Claiming God's land as your own; covetousness speaks, and God hears."},
{q:"What was Edom's fatal oversight in claiming the land?", options:["The LORD was there","The land was barren","The cities were empty","The people had fled"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:10",verse:"Because thou hast said, These two nations and these two countries shall be mine, and we will possess it; whereas the LORD was there:", insight:"'Whereas the LORD was there'; thieves forget the Owner is home."},
{q:"According to what would God judge Edom?", options:["According to thine anger, and according to thine envy","According to the law of Moses","According to the customs of nations","According to the prayers of Israel"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:11",verse:"Therefore, as I live, saith the Lord GOD, I will even do according to thine anger, and according to thine envy which thou hast used out of thy hatred against them; and I will make myself known among them, when I have judged thee.", insight:"Judged by your own anger and envy; God turns your measure back upon you."},
{q:"What would God make known when He judged Edom?", options:["Himself, among them","The secrets of Babylon","The wealth of Egypt","The sins of Judah"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:11",verse:"Therefore, as I live, saith the Lord GOD, I will even do according to thine anger, and according to thine envy which thou hast used out of thy hatred against them; and I will make myself known among them, when I have judged thee.", insight:"He will make Himself known; judgment is God's self introduction."},
{q:"What had God heard from Edom?", options:["All thy blasphemies spoken against the mountains of Israel","Their songs of praise","Their prayers for mercy","Their confessions of sin"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:12",verse:"And thou shalt know that I am the LORD, and that I have heard all thy blasphemies which thou hast spoken against the mountains of Israel, saying, They are laid desolate, they are given us to consume.", insight:"Every blasphemy heard; heaven keeps a record of words spoken against God's people."},
{q:"What did Edom say about the mountains of Israel?", options:["They are laid desolate, they are given us to consume","They are holy and untouchable","They belong to no one","They will be restored soon"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:12",verse:"And thou shalt know that I am the LORD, and that I have heard all thy blasphemies which thou hast spoken against the mountains of Israel, saying, They are laid desolate, they are given us to consume.", insight:"'Given us to consume'; gloating over ruins is blasphemy in God's ears."},
{q:"How had Edom sinned with their mouth?", options:["They boasted against God, and multiplied their words against Him","They were silent when they should speak","They prayed to other gods","They cursed their own king"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:13",verse:"Thus with your mouth ye have boasted against me, and have multiplied your words against me: I have heard them.", insight:"Boasting against God with multiplied words; pride talks, and God listens."},
{q:"When would God make Edom desolate?", options:["When the whole earth rejoiceth","When the sun stands still","When the sea runs dry","When the stars fall"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:14",verse:"Thus saith the Lord GOD; When the whole earth rejoiceth, I will make thee desolate.", insight:"While the whole earth rejoices, Edom is desolate; judgment isolates the proud."},
{q:"By what measure would God repay Edom?", options:["As thou didst rejoice at Israel's desolation, so will I do unto thee","Seven times more than Babylon suffered","With mercy and compassion","With exile but not destruction"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:15",verse:"As thou didst rejoice at the inheritance of the house of Israel, because it was desolate, so will I do unto thee: thou shalt be desolate, O mount Seir, and all Idumea, even all of it: and they shall know that I am the LORD.", insight:"Measured by your own rejoicing; the joy you took in another's ruin becomes your ruin."},
{q:"How complete would Edom's desolation be?", options:["All Idumea, even all of it","Only the border towns","Half the land","The cities but not the fields"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 35:15",verse:"As thou didst rejoice at the inheritance of the house of Israel, because it was desolate, so will I do unto thee: thou shalt be desolate, O mount Seir, and all Idumea, even all of it: and they shall know that I am the LORD.", insight:"'Even all of it'; partial hatred earns total desolation."}
]}
]);
